From: IHulkSmashI <227083792+IHulkSmashI@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:09:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Power: PL2 = PL1 + 2 W, Autotune beta and off by default,
 MangoHud only with Autotune

From an audit against the proven tools (hhd, PowerControl, PowerStation, Handheld
Companion, SimpleDeckyTDP, other tools):
- PL2 = PL1 + 2 W as hhd (adjustor/core/rapl.py), PowerControl (cpu.py) and
  PowerStation (max_boost 2.0) do; ClawDeck scaled it to 45 W at 35 W, so the
  package burst and got clamped (a likely source of noisy frame times).
- Autotune off by default and labelled beta (other tools removed its AutoTDP; Steam
  has none; the maintainer OK'd shipping it as beta or off).
- The launch wrapper injects MangoHud only while Autotune is on (its log is only
  for Autotune; Steam's overlay is already mangoapp).
- Autotune no longer trims the CPU ceiling (max_perf_pct): no proven tool does it
  and it hurts frame pacing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019jJLUgw5uVPaAcLuRF5SqW
